    "broader": "region-central-african",
    "definition": "Traditions with primary roots in Bantu and Kongo religious culture. Bantu as a linguistic and cultural family spans Central, East, and Southern Africa; this concept primarily covers the Kongo-rooted Central African traditions most prominent in Afro-Atlantic contexts. For traditions specifically rooted in Southern or East African Bantu cultures, use or add appropriate region-specific concepts under iroko:region-central-african, iroko:region-east-african, or iroko:region-southern-african.",
    "scopeNote": "Bantu spans multiple geographic regions. This concept is anchored to Central Africa / Kongo-derived Atlantic traditions. See region-east-african and region-southern-african for other Bantu-rooted traditions."
